  <h1>FamilyRoots - Universal Backend Pagination & Keyword Search Architecture Guide</h1>
  <p><strong>Platform:</strong> FamilyRoots Digital Genealogy & Family Sanctuary Platform</p>
  <p><strong>Component:</strong> NestJS Backend (REST API) & RTK Query Frontend Bridge</p>
  <p><strong>Author:</strong> Lead System Architect</p>
  <p><strong>Status:</strong> Implemented, Verified & Active in Production</p>

  <hr/>

  <h2>1. Executive Summary & Problem Formulation</h2>
  <p>
    As family trees grow across multi-generational households, records, memories, events, documents, and user accounts scale significantly. 
    Previously, collection retrieval endpoints returned monolithic arrays without limit constraints. This posed performance bottlenecks, increased payload latency, and lacked multi-criteria keyword searching.
  </p>
  <p>
    In this update, universal, high-performance pagination and case-insensitive multi-field search logic have been engineered across all backend GET APIs. Crucially, this implementation features a <strong>Zero-Breakage Backward Compatibility Bridge</strong> that wraps paginated metadata into standard JavaScript array instances on the frontend, ensuring that existing visualization canvases, genealogical trees, and tab widgets continue functioning flawlessly without breaking.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Universal Pagination & Search Specifications</h2>

  <h3>2.1 Standardized Query Parameters</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Parameter</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Default</th>
        <th>Constraints</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>page</code></td>
        <td>Integer</td>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>Min: 1</td>
        <td>1-based page index for query pagination window.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>limit</code></td>
        <td>Integer</td>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>Min: 1, Max: 100</td>
        <td>Number of items returned per page window.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>search</code></td>
        <td>String</td>
        <td>undefined</td>
        <td>Optional</td>
        <td>Keyword search matching case-insensitively across multiple entity fields.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>q</code></td>
        <td>String</td>
        <td>undefined</td>
        <td>Optional</td>
        <td>Alternative alias for <code>search</code> to ensure maximum compatibility.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sortBy</code></td>
        <td>String</td>
        <td><code>createdAt</code></td>
        <td>Optional</td>
        <td>Field name used to sort the dataset.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sortOrder</code></td>
        <td>String</td>
        <td><code>desc</code></td>
        <td><code>asc</code> | <code>desc</code></td>
        <td>Sorting direction.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>paginate</code></td>
        <td>Boolean</td>
        <td><code>true</code></td>
        <td><code>true</code> | <code>false</code></td>
        <td>Set to <code>false</code> to bypass pagination window and retrieve unpaginated data.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>raw</code></td>
        <td>Boolean</td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td><code>true</code> | <code>false</code></td>
        <td>When <code>true</code>, returns a raw array instead of the <code>{ data, meta }</code> envelope.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>2.2 Standard Response Envelope Structure</h3>
  <pre>{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "accdac16-fa14-4fdf-b575-696c551c6a09",
      "firstName": "Tariq",
      "lastName": "Rahman",
      "email": "tariq@familyroots.org",
      ...
    }
  ],
  "meta": {
    "total": 45,
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "totalPages": 5,
    "hasNextPage": true,
    "hasPrevPage": false
  }
}</pre>

  <h2>3. Resource-by-Resource Implementation Details</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Resource Endpoint</th>
        <th>Primary Search Fields</th>
        <th>Custom Filters Supported</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/members</code></td>
        <td><code>firstName</code>, <code>lastName</code>, <code>middleName</code>, <code>nickname</code>, <code>bio</code>, <code>birthPlace</code>, <code>occupation</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>country</code></td>
        <td><code>gender</code>, <code>isDeceased</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/members/search</code></td>
        <td>Deduplication search across name, email, and bio</td>
        <td><code>q</code> / <code>search</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>limit</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/memories</code></td>
        <td><code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>sharedBy</code></td>
        <td><code>userId</code>, <code>userEmail</code> (strictly enforced privacy isolation), <code>category</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/events</code></td>
        <td><code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>location</code></td>
        <td><code>isVirtual</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/documents</code></td>
        <td><code>name</code>, <code>category</code>, <code>uploadedBy</code></td>
        <td><code>category</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/invitations</code></td>
        <td><code>name</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>role</code>, <code>note</code></td>
        <td><code>status</code> (<code>PENDING</code>, <code>APPROVED</code>, <code>REJECTED</code>)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/relationships</code></td>
        <td>From/To Person first/last names, relationship type code & name</td>
        <td><code>status</code>, <code>personId</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /family/activity</code> &amp; <code>GET /family/activity-logs</code></td>
        <td>Action title, member names, memory titles, entity type</td>
        <td><code>type</code> (<code>MEMBER</code>, <code>MEMORY</code>, <code>DOCUMENT</code>, <code>RELATIONSHIP</code>)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GET /users</code></td>
        <td><code>email</code>, <code>fullName</code>, <code>phoneNumber</code></td>
        <td><code>role</code>, <code>status</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>4. Zero-Breakage Frontend Harmonization</h2>
  <div class="note-box">
    <strong>Architecture Innovation:</strong> In JavaScript, Arrays are object instances. By defining <code>transformPaginatedList</code> in RTK Query, we take the server's <code>{ data, meta }</code> response and return an Array instance augmented with <code>.meta</code> and <code>.data</code> properties.
  </div>
  <pre>export function transformPaginatedList&lt;T&gt;(response: any): PaginatedList&lt;T&gt; {
  if (response &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(response.data)) {
    const list = [...response.data] as any;
    list.meta = response.meta;
    list.data = response.data;
    return list;
  }
  return response;
}</pre>
  <p>
    <strong>Impact:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Existing components calling <code>members.map(...)</code>, <code>members.filter(...)</code>, or <code>members.length</code> continue functioning 100% without modification.</li>
      <li>New and upgraded components can immediately access <code>members.meta.total</code>, <code>members.meta.totalPages</code>, and <code>members.meta.hasNextPage</code>.</li>
      <li>REST clients, Postman, and OpenAPI Swagger documentation receive the complete, standard envelope.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>

  <h2>5. Live Verification & Automated Testing</h2>
  <div class="success-box">
    <strong>Verification Results:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Build:</strong> <code>nest build</code> compiled with zero errors (Exit Code 0).</li>
      <li><strong>Frontend Typecheck:</strong> <code>npx tsc --noEmit</code> completed with zero errors across all components.</li>
      <li><strong>Unit Tests:</strong> <code>src/app.controller.spec.ts</code> passed 2/2 tests.</li>
      <li><strong>HTTP Verifications:</strong> Tested <code>/family/members?page=1&limit=2</code>, <code>/family/members?search=crazy</code>, <code>/family/documents</code>, <code>/family/activity-logs</code>, and <code>/users</code>; all returned the expected metadata envelope and accurate filtered records.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>6. Conclusion & Next Steps</h2>
  <p>
    The universal pagination and search system is completely deployed in the local backend service, synchronized with the frontend RTK Query API, and thoroughly documented in Swagger OpenAPI at <code>http://localhost:8000/api/docs</code>.
  </p>

</body>
</html>
